    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who headline our daily efficiency ratings at 83.29 and 82.95, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** is the standout play; he benefits from an optimal matchup against Avila, whose 4.91 xERA is amplified by a park factor providing a +16% boost to his offensive output. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is a high-conviction start at 75.10, thriving despite a moderate park penalty because he faces a vulnerable arm in Bieber (5.69 xERA) and carries a significant dynamic platoon edge. We are also leaning heavily into speed-dependent upside today; **Josh Lowe** (68.71) and **Andy Pages** (74.01) are prioritized due to their ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries, a critical component for closing the gap in our scarcity-driven SB category.\n\nOur most difficult roster construction choice involved the final bench spots, where **Heliot Ramos** (54.25) was the strongest omission. While **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a helpful wind and a potential SB opportunity against Gordon\u2019s slow delivery, he was ultimately edged out by the superior consistency and higher daily floor provided by **Miguel Vargas** and **Drake Baldwin**. **Miguel Vargas** remains a lock in the utility spot with an elite 0.402 xwOBA, while **Drake Baldwin** earns the start at catcher due to favorable SP-specific factors. We remain vigilant regarding the lineup fluidity for our remaining bench depth, including **Jacob Wilson** and **Wade Meckler**; while their scores are currently sub-60, any shifts in order or late-breaking weather patterns could warrant a pivot to capitalize on their specific platoon advantages later in the day.",
